<description><![CDATA[DEM: USGS 3DEP 3DEPElevation ImageServer exportImage, bbox -104.62,29.72,-103.86,30.40, 2736x2448 px (~1 arcsec), bilinear, retrieved 2026-09-28. Eye 1.6 m; headlight target 0.7 m; terrain sampled every 15 m; last 60 m before each target excluded (road-bed smoothing). 'Marginal' = clears distant terrain by <= 5 m, or blocked only by ground within 1 km of the car, where a 30 m DEM is unreliable. Colour = minimum refraction coefficient k needed to see a 0.7 m headlight. k = 503·P/T²·(0.0343 + dT/dz) (Hirt et al. 2010); at P≈850 hPa, T≈283 K: k 0.13 ≈ standard lapse, k 0.5 ≈ +0.06 K/m, k 1.0 ≈ +0.15 K/m inversion. Constant-k is an approximation; near-ground gradients vary with height.]]></description>
